==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|orv|ru}} {{term|вѣдѣ|lang=orv}}. Russian [[ведь]] is a former {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} root [[perfect tense|perfect]] {{m|ine-pro|*wóyd-}} with [[mediopassive]] ending ''-ai'', with meaning "I have seen". Cognate with {{etyl|en|-}} [[wit]] (to wit).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-pron-auto|ведь}}
* {{audio|Ru-ведь.ogg|audio|lang=ru}}

===Interjection===
{{head|ru|interjection}}

# [[after all]]
# [[indeed]], [[surely]]
# [[why]], [[well]]
# [[then]], you know, you see
# isn’t it?
#:* {{lang|ru|Ведь [[уже#Russian|уже́]] [[поздно|по́здно]]}} — ''It’s late, isn’t it?''
#:* {{lang|ru|Ведь [[он#Russian|он]] [[знаток|знато́к]]}} — ''After all, he’s an expert.''
#:* {{lang|ru|Ведь [[я#Russian|я]] [[вы|вам]] [[говорить|говори́л]]!}} — ''But I told you!''

===Conjunction===
{{head|ru|conjunction}}

# you see, [[you know]]
#:* {{lang|ru|[[он#Russian|Он]] [[лежать|лежи́т]], ведь он [[на#Russian|на]] [[прошлый|про́шлой]] [[неделя#Russian|неде́ле]] [[заболеть|заболе́л]]}} — ''He’s in bed...he fell ill last week, you know.''

